  "executive_briefing": "Global tax and trade policy frameworks in late 2026 are undergoing critical structural transitions. The aggressive worldwide integration of the OECD Pillar Two 15% global minimum tax is reshaping corporate tax strategies across more than 140 jurisdictions. To balance global compliance with local competitiveness, regions like ASEAN are restructuring incentives, exemplified by Singapore's statutory rate stability paired with target CIT rebates. In digital tax compliance, continuous transaction controls are maturing as Singapore outlines firm, phased mandatory timelines for its Peppol-based InvoiceNow system. Meanwhile, unilateral trade policies face intense scrutiny, with the U.S. Court of International Trade declaring certain emergency-power tariffs unlawful, even as threat of escalating reciprocal tariffs persists.",
